// Assuming WDT_REG_KEY and WDT_FEED_VALUE are defined
void feed_watchdog_timer() {
    // This function should be called periodically from the main application loop
    // or a high-level task that reflects overall system health.
    WDT_REG_KEY = WDT_FEED_VALUE; 
}
```
**Common Pitfall Avoided:** Feeding the WDT from an Interrupt Service Routine (ISR) or a low-priority task. This snippet implies feeding from the main application logic, which is crucial because an ISR might still execute even if the main application loop is stuck, giving a false sense of system health.
